---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy - designedbykoda"
	description="How designedbykoda collects, uses, and protects your data."
>
	<div class="policy-page">
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="updated">Last updated: 13 November 2026</p>

		<p>
			In this policy, "we", "us" and "our" mean designedbykoda, run by
			Dylan Haines (ABN 61 261 672 813), which makes designedbykoda.com and the E-Ink Calendar. "You" means anyone who
			uses the website, the dashboard or an E-Ink Calendar, or places a pre-order.
		</p>

		<p>
			This policy explains what information designedbykoda collects, how it is used, and
			the choices you have, specifically in relation to the E-Ink Calendar product and its
			connection to your Google Calendar and, if you choose to use the To-do layout, your Google Tasks. If you have questions after reading this, contact
			us at <a href="mailto:hello@designedbykoda.com">hello@designedbykoda.com</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
		<p>When you connect your Google account to set up an E-Ink Calendar device, we collect:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Your Google account email address and a unique account identifier, used to identify your account.</li>
			<li>Read only access to the Google Calendar or calendars you choose to connect, including event titles, start times, and whether an event is marked as an all day event.</li>
			<li>A device identifier and a device authentication credential, generated by your physical device during setup.</li>
			<li>Basic device settings you configure, such as your timezone and how often the device should refresh.</li>
			<li>Optional display settings you choose, such as the location used for weather, sunrise, sunset and moon times, the name and date for a Countdown, and a picture you upload for the Photo frame layout. An uploaded picture is converted to a small black and white image in your browser, and only that converted image is stored.</li>
			<li>Other things you set up for your screen: a schedule of which screen shows when, your language, temperature unit and clock, the words on the Meeting room, Guest welcome and Desk name plate screens (for Guest welcome this can include a Wi-Fi network name and password, which are shown on the screen as a QR code), repeating reminders, and screen designs you make in the layout builder.</li>
			<li>Messages sent to your calendar: the text, an optional name typed by the sender, when it was sent and when it expires. Messages can be sent from your dashboard, or by anyone you give your calendar's shared message link to. That link contains a random secret; you can turn it off or replace it at any time, and it stops working straight away.</li>
			<li>If you share a screen design, a copy of it can be seen by anyone with the link, and they can add it to their own calendar. Wi-Fi names and passwords are left out of that copy, and it never includes your events, messages, photos or name. Stopping sharing turns the link off straight away.</li>
			<li>Information your device reports when it checks in: its battery voltage (kept as a history so the dashboard can show a battery graph and estimate how long a charge lasts), its firmware version, when it last checked in, which screen it last showed and when it will next update.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			If you choose the To-do layout, you are asked separately to grant read only access to
			your Google Tasks. This is only requested at that point, not when you first connect your
			calendar. When your device refreshes, our server reads the titles, due dates and
			completion status of the tasks in your default Google Tasks list so they can be drawn on
			the screen. Your tasks are not saved in our database; they are used to build the
			screen image and then discarded.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you vote in a poll on this site, we store your choices together with a random
			identifier saved in a cookie in your browser, and a one-way hash (it cannot be reversed)
			of your network address and browser type. These are used only so that voting again
			replaces your earlier vote instead of counting twice. Your name, email and address are
			not stored with your vote.
		</p>
		<p>
			We do not request or receive access to any other Google service. We do not request
			permission to create, edit, or delete anything in your calendar or your tasks. All
			access is read only. Marking a task as done is done in Google Tasks or Google
			Calendar, not through our service.
		</p>

		<h2>Pre-orders and Payments</h2>
		<p>
			When you pre-order, payment is handled by Stripe. You enter your card details on
			Stripe's checkout page and they go straight to Stripe; we never see or store your
			full card number. From your order we receive and keep:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Your name, email address, phone number and shipping address.</li>
			<li>What you ordered, the amount paid, the currency and the shipping cost.</li>
			<li>The order's progress once it ships, such as the date it was posted and its tracking number.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			We use this only to make and deliver your order, to contact you about it (for example
			if there is a delay or a problem with your address), to handle any refund, and to keep
			the business records the law requires. Your address is given to Australia Post
			to deliver your order. Order details are kept for as long as Australian
			tax law requires us to keep business records (currently five years), then deleted.
		</p>

		<h2>How We Use This Information</h2>
		<p>The information above is used for one purpose: to let your physical E-Ink Calendar device retrieve your upcoming events (and, if you choose the To-do layout, your tasks) and display them on its screen. Specifically:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Your Google account identifier links your device to your calendar selection.</li>
			<li>Your calendar data, and your task data if you use the To-do layout, is fetched by our server and passed to your device in a simplified format it can render.</li>
			<li>Your timezone setting is used to correctly calculate what day it is for you and when your device should refresh.</li>
			<li>Messages, reminders and the other things you set up are used only to draw your screen and to show them back to you in your dashboard.</li>
			<li>Battery readings are used only to show your calendar's battery level, graph and estimated time left.</li>
			<li>Your Google account email is used to link pre-orders you paid for with the same email to your account, and to send the email alerts you choose (battery low, a calendar that stops checking in, or an update). You can turn each alert off on your dashboard or with the link in any alert email. Alert emails are sent through Brevo.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			We do not use your data for advertising, do not build behavioural profiles from it,
			and do not sell it to any third party.
		</p>
		<p>
			Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs, including Google
			Calendar and Google Tasks, adheres to the
			<a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
			including the Limited Use requirements. Data from Google is used only to provide the
			display feature described above. It is not used to develop, improve or train
			generalised AI or machine learning models, and no person at designedbykoda reads your
			calendar events or tasks, except where you ask us for support and give permission, or
			where the law requires it.
		</p>

		<h2>Data Storage and Security</h2>
		<p>We take the following specific steps to protect your data:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>The refresh token that grants access to your Google Calendar and Google Tasks is encrypted before it is stored. It is never stored in plain text.</li>
			<li>Your device's authentication credential is never stored directly. Only a one way cryptographic hash of it is kept, so the original value cannot be recovered even if our database were accessed.</li>
			<li>All data is stored using Cloudflare's infrastructure, and all communication between your device, your browser, and our servers happens over encrypted connections.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Third Party Services</h2>
		<p>To operate the E-Ink Calendar, we rely on a small number of service providers:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Google</strong>, to authenticate your account and retrieve your calendar and task data. Google's own privacy policy applies to how they handle your account information.</li>
			<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts our website, database, and server infrastructure.</li>
			<li><strong>Stripe</strong>, which processes pre-order payments. Stripe's privacy policy applies to the payment details you give them.</li>
			<li><strong>Australia Post</strong>, who receive your name and shipping address to deliver your order.</li>
			<li><strong>Open-Meteo</strong>, a weather service. If you set a location for weather, its coordinates are sent to Open-Meteo to get the forecast. No account details or calendar data are sent.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			If you join a waitlist for one of our products, your email address is stored with
			Brevo, our email service provider, solely to send you updates about that product.
		</p>

		<h2>Your Rights and Choices</h2>
		<p>You are in control of the access you grant us at all times:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>You can revoke our access to your Google Calendar and Google Tasks at any time from your own Google Account settings, at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. This immediately stops us from being able to access your calendar or tasks.</li>
			<li>You can delete your account and all associated data at any time from the bottom of your dashboard, or by contacting <a href="mailto:hello@designedbykoda.com">hello@designedbykoda.com</a>.</li>
			<li>You can unpair a device from your dashboard. Unpairing deletes that device's settings, messages, reminders, designs and battery history.</li>
			<li>You can unsubscribe from any waitlist email using the link included in that email.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Data Retention</h2>
		<p>
			We retain your account information for as long as your device remains active and
			connected. If you delete your account or revoke access, we delete the associated
			encrypted refresh token and stop retrieving calendar and task data on your behalf. Everything stored for your devices (settings, pictures, Countdown details, messages, reminders, designs and battery history) is deleted with your account, or when you unpair that device. Removed and expired messages stay stored until then, so they can be shown in your message history. Battery history older than 90 days is deleted automatically.
		</p>

		<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			The E-Ink Calendar is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect
			information from anyone under the age of 13.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
		<p>
			If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a
			revised date at the top.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			For any questions about this policy or your data, contact
			<a href="mailto:hello@designedbykoda.com">hello@designedbykoda.com</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.policy-page {
		max-width: 680px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 3em 0 5em 0;
	}
	.policy-page h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0.3em;
	}
	.updated {
		color: var(--muted-dim);
		font-size: 0.9em;
		margin-bottom: 2em;
	}
	.policy-page h2 {
		font-size: 1.2em;
		margin-top: 2em;
		margin-bottom: 0.6em;
	}
	.policy-page p {
		color: var(--muted);
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin-bottom: 1em;
	}
	.policy-page ul {
		color: var(--muted);
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin-bottom: 1em;
		padding-left: 1.3em;
	}
	.policy-page li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	.policy-page a {
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.policy-page strong {
		color: var(--fg);
	}
</style>
